touch-keyboard (1.5.0+yb1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Disable the Halo touch keyboard while the printed keys are out of reach.
    The two halves of the machine are joined by a 360-degree hinge and the
    embedded controller reports the angle between them through hid-sensor-hub
    ("hinge" channel).  Below 10 degrees the machine is folded shut, above
    180 degrees it is unfolded past the keyboard (flat on the desk is about
    178, folded round behind is about 360 reported as 0); in both poses
    touches on the printed keyboard are accidental and are no longer turned
    into keystrokes.  Poses are applied with a 5 degree hysteresis band so
    moving the machine cannot flicker the gate, held keys are released on
    leaving a usable pose, and the gate stays open if no sensor is present.
  * Locate that sensor by the label of its first angle channel
    (in_angl0_label == hinge) instead of by an iio:deviceN number, which
    follows probe order.
  * CMakeLists.txt: do not let pkg_get_variable() overwrite an explicitly
    configured SYSTEMD_SYSTEM_UNIT_DIR when the systemd pkg-config module is
    absent, and fall back to /usr/lib/systemd/system.
  * Add hinge_monitor_test exercising the pose thresholds and the hysteresis
    boundaries.

 -- Michal Bicz <michal@bicz.net>  Thu, 16 Oct 2026 21:05:00 -0700

touch-keyboard (1.4.9+yb1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Install libinput quirk file 61-yogabook.quirks: opt the virtual-touchpad
    out of tablet-mode suspension (ModelTabletModeNoSuspend).  libinput
    pairs the internal virtual touchpad with the pulsed virtual
    tablet-mode switch and suspends it while the switch is ON, which
    froze the trackpad 5 seconds after every handler (re)start.  The
    switch itself keeps working for mutter touch mode (auto-rotation).
  * touch-keyboard-handler.service: Restart=always with RestartSec=1 and
    StartLimitIntervalSec=0, so a Goodix source-device disappearance
    (halo mode switch rebinds) no longer leaves the trackpad dead until
    the next udev re-add.

 -- Michal Bicz <michal@bicz.net>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 11:20:00 +0200

touch-keyboard (1.4.8+yb3) unstable; urgency=medium
  * Add a dedicated virtual-tablet-switch uinput device that reports
    SW_TABLET_MODE so GNOME/mutter keeps touch mode (auto-rotation)
    enabled while the halo strip pointer device exists.  The Yoga Book
    YB1-X90F has no physical tablet-mode switch, and mutter disables
    touch mode whenever a pointer is present without one.  The switch
    is pulsed OFF->ON periodically because mutter only updates touch
    mode on toggle events; a touchpad+switch combo device would not
    work since libinput's touchpad path returns before evaluating the
    switch tag.

 -- Michal Bicz <michal@bicz.net>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0200

